{"seq":3,"slug":"underwater-caustics","title":"水下与焦散","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/game-water-rendering/shading/underwater-caustics","wordCount":1677,"readingTime":7,"html":"<h1 id=\"水下与焦散\">水下与焦散</h1><p>前两篇都站在水面之上往下看。但很多游戏要把镜头沉进水里——潜水、沉船、水下关卡——这时光的故事换了讲法：你身处一个会吸光、会散射的介质中，远处的一切被蓝绿色的雾吞没，阳光从波动的水面斜射下来形成一根根可见的光柱，而水底铺满了一张晃动的、网状的明亮光斑。这张光斑就是焦散（caustics），是水下场景最具标志性的视觉签名。本篇讲水面之下的三件事：水下雾与能见度、体积光（god rays）、以及焦散的生成。它复用了 <a href=\"fresnel-depth\">菲涅尔与深度色</a> 的吸收模型，只是把观察者放进了水里，并为整章的光路收尾。</p>\n<h2 id=\"核心概念\">核心概念</h2><ul>\n<li><strong>水下雾</strong>：吸收直接作用于相机到物体的水中距离，本质是 <a href=\"fresnel-depth\">Beer-Lambert</a> 的指数雾，参数（雾色、密度）随浑浊度调，成本极低却效果决定性。</li>\n<li><strong>体积光（丁达尔）</strong>：阳光被水中悬浮微粒散射使光路本身可见，有光轴 ray-march、屏幕空间径向模糊、手摆光柱片三档；ray-march 会被波形/障碍切割出动态明暗条纹，最可信。</li>\n<li><strong>焦散</strong>：起伏水面像一组动态透镜把阳光会聚成水底网状亮纹，从滚动贴图到实时法线生成（与波形 Jacobian 相通）到屏幕空间/光追三档。</li>\n<li><strong>同根</strong>：三者都源于&quot;水是吸收并散射光的介质&quot;，全开属影视级，但只要有水下玩法，加一点点可信度就断崖式提升。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"水下雾-把吸收反过来用\">水下雾：把吸收反过来用</h2><p>水面之上看水，吸收作用于&quot;折射进去再出来&quot;的光；潜到水下，吸收直接作用于你到每个物体之间的视线。所以水下雾本质上就是 <a href=\"fresnel-depth\">菲涅尔与深度色</a> 那套 Beer-Lambert 吸收，只不过距离 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span></span></span></span></span> 变成了相机到物体的水中距离：</p>\n<div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mtext> </mtext><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mtext> </mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C = C_{object}\\, e^{-\\sigma_\\lambda d} + C_{water}\\,(1 - e^{-\\sigma_\\lambda d})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1852em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">o</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0572em;\">bj</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">ec</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8991em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">σ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3448em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.3488em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">λ</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1512em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">er</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1491em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8991em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">σ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3448em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.3488em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.0714em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.5em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">λ</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1512em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span></div><p>近处物体清晰，远处迅速被水体颜色吞没并褪成蓝绿。<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma_\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">σ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">λ</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 仍是红 &gt; 绿 &gt; 蓝的波长相关吸收，于是水下世界天然偏青蓝。工程上这通常就是一个基于水中距离的指数雾，参数（雾色、密度）随水的浑浊度调；浑水加大散射、清水减小。这一步成本极低却效果决定性——少了它，水下场景看起来只是&quot;调蓝的陆地&quot;。</p>\n<h2 id=\"体积光-可见的光柱\">体积光：可见的光柱</h2><p>晴天潜水，你会看到一束束从水面斜插下来的光柱，这是阳光被水中悬浮微粒散射、让光路本身可见，即体积光或丁达尔效应。在游戏里它有两类常见实现，下表对比。</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>方法</th>\n<th>原理</th>\n<th>质量/成本</th>\n<th>适用</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>光轴 ray-march</td>\n<td>沿视线步进，按到光源的能见度累加散射</td>\n<td>高质量、较贵</td>\n<td>主机/PC 关键水下场景</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>屏幕空间径向模糊</td>\n<td>从屏幕上光源位置做径向 blur</td>\n<td>便宜、易穿帮</td>\n<td>移动端、远景近似</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>半透明光柱片</td>\n<td>手摆几片带噪声的发光网格</td>\n<td>最便宜、可控</td>\n<td>风格化、固定机位</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>ray-march 版本每步检查该点是否被遮挡（在阴影里就没光散射出来），所以光柱会被水面波形、礁石、沉船切割出动态的明暗条纹，最为可信。无论哪种，体积光都要和水下雾配合：雾提供了散射介质的&quot;密度感&quot;，光柱是这层介质里被照亮的部分。</p>\n<h2 id=\"焦散-水面当透镜\">焦散：水面当透镜</h2><p>焦散是水下最迷人的一笔：起伏的水面像一组连续变化的透镜，把平行的阳光时而会聚、时而发散，投到水底就成了一张不断游动的网状亮纹。它的物理是光线经水面折射后的能量重新分布——会聚处变亮、发散处变暗。真实计算焦散要追踪大量光线经水面折射后打在哪里（光子映射或光线追踪），实时游戏几乎都用近似，下面是三档常见做法。</p>\n<p>最便宜的一档是焦散贴图：预先做好（或用一段循环动画）一张网状焦散纹理，把它投影到水底表面，再随时间滚动/混合两层 UV 制造流动感，并按 <a href=\"fresnel-depth\">水下与深度色</a> 的水深调制强度（浅处亮、深处弱）。中档是从实际水面法线/位移实时生成焦散：用 <a href=\"../waves/\">波形</a> 章的法线计算光线折射后的汇聚度（和 Gerstner/FFT 的 Jacobian 概念相通——收缩处即会聚处即亮纹）。最高档是 2026 年高端项目才用的屏幕空间或光线追踪焦散，质量最好但成本高。</p>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"flowchart\" data-source=\"flowchart TD&#10;  SUN[阳光] --&gt; SURF[起伏水面:透镜组]&#10;  SURF --&gt; CONV[折射后会聚/发散]&#10;  CONV --&gt; FLOOR[水底:网状焦散亮纹]&#10;  CAM[水下相机] --&gt; FOG[水下雾:Beer-Lambert吸收]&#10;  CAM --&gt; GR[体积光:被遮挡切割的光柱]&#10;  FLOOR --&gt; FOG&#10;  GR --&gt; FOG&#10;  FOG --&gt; OUT[水下画面]\">flowchart TD\n  SUN[阳光] --&gt; SURF[起伏水面:透镜组]\n  SURF --&gt; CONV[折射后会聚/发散]\n  CONV --&gt; FLOOR[水底:网状焦散亮纹]\n  CAM[水下相机] --&gt; FOG[水下雾:Beer-Lambert吸收]\n  CAM --&gt; GR[体积光:被遮挡切割的光柱]\n  FLOOR --&gt; FOG\n  GR --&gt; FOG\n  FOG --&gt; OUT[水下画面]</pre><h2 id=\"把三者编织起来\">把三者编织起来</h2><p>一个可信的水下镜头是三层叠加：底层是被焦散点亮、又被水下雾按距离染蓝的场景，中层是切割光柱的体积光，整体笼罩在随浑浊度变化的蓝绿色调里。三者都根植于同一个事实——水是吸收并散射光的介质，焦散是水面对入射光的重分布，雾是视线方向的吸收，体积光是介质里被照亮的部分。它们成本不低，是技术谱系里&quot;影视级&quot;档才全开的内容（见 <a href=\"../foundations/water-techniques-spectrum\">技术谱系</a>），但只要有水下玩法，哪怕只加一张滚动焦散贴图和一个水下雾，可信度就会断崖式提升。本篇也为整个 <a href=\"./\">着色</a> 章画上句号：从水面反射折射、到菲涅尔深度色、再到水下焦散，光从打上水面到沉入水底的完整旅程讲完了。</p>\n<h2 id=\"小结\">小结</h2><ul>\n<li>水下雾是 Beer-Lambert 吸收用在相机到物体的水中距离上，红 &gt; 绿 &gt; 蓝吸收让水下天然偏青蓝，成本极低却决定性。</li>\n<li>体积光（丁达尔）有 ray-march、屏幕空间径向模糊、手摆光柱片三档；ray-march 会被波形/障碍切割出动态明暗条纹最可信。</li>\n<li>焦散是水面当透镜把阳光重分布成网状亮纹，从滚动贴图到实时法线生成（与 Jacobian 相通）到光追三档。</li>\n<li>三者同根于&quot;水是吸收并散射光的介质&quot;，全开属影视级，但任何水下玩法加一点都回报巨大。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"延伸阅读\">延伸阅读</h2><ul>\n<li>同章上一篇：<a href=\"fresnel-depth\">菲涅尔与深度色</a> —— 水下雾复用的正是这里的吸收模型。</li>\n<li>上游：<a href=\"../waves/gerstner-waves\">Gerstner 波</a> —— 焦散会聚度与波形 Jacobian 同源。</li>\n<li>跨库：<a href=\"../../game-lighting-global-illumination/global-illumination/realtime-gi\">全局光照 · 实时 GI</a> —— 体积光与水下间接光照的相邻技术。</li>\n<li>跨库：<a href=\"../../shader-programming/advanced-effects/procedural-noise\">着色器编程 · 程序化噪声</a> —— 焦散贴图与光柱噪声的程序化来源。</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"level":1,"text":"水下与焦散","id":"水下与焦散"},{"level":2,"text":"核心概念","id":"核心概念"},{"level":2,"text":"水下雾：把吸收反过来用","id":"水下雾-把吸收反过来用"},{"level":2,"text":"体积光：可见的光柱","id":"体积光-可见的光柱"},{"level":2,"text":"焦散：水面当透镜","id":"焦散-水面当透镜"},{"level":2,"text":"把三者编织起来","id":"把三者编织起来"},{"level":2,"text":"小结","id":"小结"},{"level":2,"text":"延伸阅读","id":"延伸阅读"}],"prev":{"title":"菲涅尔与深度色","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/game-water-rendering/shading/fresnel-depth"},"next":{"title":"交互与泡沫","url":"/l-doc-books/h/game-development/game-water-rendering/practice/interaction-foam"}}